@page "/docs/components/color-picker"

<Seo Canonical="/docs/components/color-picker" Title="Blazorise ColorPicker component" Description="Learn to use and work with the Blazorise ColorPicker component that allows you to select a color using a variety of input methods." />

<DocsPageTitle Path="Components/Color Picker">
    Blazorise ColorPicker component
</DocsPageTitle>

<DocsPageLead>
    <Code>ColorPicker</Code> helps users choose precise colors and transparency for themes, drawing tools, and other visual settings.
</DocsPageLead>

<DocsPageParagraph>
    Use the color surface to explore shades, choose a familiar color from the palette, or enter an exact color code.
    For the browser's built-in color selection dialog, use <Anchor To="docs/components/color-input" Title="Link to ColorInput">ColorInput</Anchor>.
</DocsPageParagraph>

<DocsPageSectionTitle>
    Examples
</DocsPageSectionTitle>

<DocsPageSection>
    <DocsPageSectionHeader Title="Basic">
        Bind <Code>Value</Code> to update the color as users select it. Save confirms the current color and closes the picker, Cancel restores the color from when the picker opened, and Clear removes the color.
        Use <Code>ShowSaveButton</Code>, <Code>ShowCancelButton</Code>, and <Code>ShowClearButton</Code> to control which actions are available.
    </DocsPageSectionHeader>
    <DocsPageSectionContent Code="ColorPickerExample" Outlined FullWidth>
        <ColorPickerExample />
    </DocsPageSectionContent>
</DocsPageSection>

<DocsPageSection>
    <DocsPageSectionHeader Title="Hue slider">
        In this Blazorise example, the <Code>ColorPicker</Code> component is enhanced with a hue slider, as indicated by the <Code>ShowHueSlider</Code> attribute.
    </DocsPageSectionHeader>
    <DocsPageSectionContent Code="ColorPickerShowHueExample" Outlined FullWidth>
        <ColorPickerShowHueExample />
    </DocsPageSectionContent>
</DocsPageSection>

<DocsPageSection>
    <DocsPageSectionHeader Title="Value visibility">
        Set <Code>ShowValue="false"</Code> to hide the selected color value and display only the swatch, while preserving the picker's width and swatch alignment.
    </DocsPageSectionHeader>
    <DocsPageSectionContent Code="ColorPickerShowValueExample" Outlined FullWidth>
        <ColorPickerShowValueExample />
    </DocsPageSectionContent>
</DocsPageSection>

<DocsPageSection>
    <DocsPageSectionHeader Title="Custom preview">
        Use <Code>PreviewContent</Code> to replace the swatch with an icon or other non-interactive content. Clicking the preview opens the picker. <Code>ShowValue</Code> independently controls the selected color text. Supply an accessible name when the preview has no visible label.
    </DocsPageSectionHeader>
    <DocsPageSectionContent Code="ColorPickerPreviewContentExample" Outlined FullWidth>
        <ColorPickerPreviewContentExample />
    </DocsPageSectionContent>
</DocsPageSection>

<DocsPageSection>
    <DocsPageSectionHeader Title="Animation" New>
        The picker menu fades in when opened and closes immediately. Set <Code>Animated="false"</Code> to open immediately, or use <Code>AnimationDuration</Code> to adjust the opening duration in milliseconds.
        A null duration preserves the provider's default; zero or a negative value disables the animation. The user's reduced-motion preference is respected automatically.
    </DocsPageSectionHeader>
    <DocsPageSectionContent Code="ColorPickerAnimationExample" Outlined FullWidth>
        <ColorPickerAnimationExample />
    </DocsPageSectionContent>
</DocsPageSection>

<DocsPageSectionTitle>
    Best Practices
</DocsPageSectionTitle>

<DocsPageSubsectionTitle IncludeInToc="false">
    Support Precise Choices
</DocsPageSubsectionTitle>

<DocsPageParagraph>
    Use a clear label and show the resulting color value when precision or reuse matters. Offer a sensible initial color and, when appropriate, a way to return to the product default.
</DocsPageParagraph>

<DocsPageSubsectionTitle IncludeInToc="false">
    Color Contrast
</DocsPageSubsectionTitle>

<DocsPageParagraph>
    Validate the contrast of user-selected foreground and background colors before applying them to text or controls. When the full picker interface is unnecessary, use the more compact <Anchor To="docs/components/color-input">ColorInput</Anchor> component.
</DocsPageParagraph>

